Subject: [PATCH 15/26] Decode attention round 3: G6_ATTN_ABS2 / VP2 / QT /
 FRONT / CTX4 (exact, default off); attnk bench vs round 2

absorb_m2 (G6_ATTN_ABS2=1|2|4|8): absorb_m with R outputs per warp (R weight rows in flight per lane), the q_b rows staged
with one 16 B load per thread (absorb_m's staging loop was one 2 B load per round trip), the rope on its own block column.
value_project_m2 (G6_ATTN_VP2=1|2|4): the same for value_project_m, float4 context staging unrolled. Per output the same
fmaf chain, warp_sum and store.
G6_ATTN_QT=1: run_body's absorb_m2 stores q / rope lane-transposed and scores_sc_qt reads a head's query with 4 + 1 vector
loads instead of 18 (and a slot's KV scales with one); the same values in the same registers.
G6_ATTN_FRONT=1: append_kv, append_index and prep_index (full layer) or append_kv and reuse (shared) in one launch
(attn_front); the bodies moved into __device__ functions, the kernels call them.
context_pk4 (G6_ATTN_CTX4=1|2|3): context_pk3 with the batches' KV bytes gathered into a shared ring by cp.async, NS-1
batches ahead.
Flags 0: the SASS of every existing kernel matches the build without this change (attnk build, 262 functions).
